{'sentiment score': -0.35, 'confidence': 0.05, 'reason': 'This schedule shows the supplemental cash flow information related to leases.\n\nThe main concepts and relationships in this schedule are:\n1. Noncurrent deferred tax asset liability: This represents the difference between the carrying value of an asset and its recoverable amount plus any applicable adjustments, as measured by FAS 157.\n2. Deferred Tax Liabilities, Gross: This is the total amount of deferred tax liabilities, including both current and non-current components.\n3. Less: Valuation allowance: This represents the portion of deferred tax liabilities that should not be recognized due to uncertainty about future recoverability of assets.\n4. Deferred Tax Liabilities, net: This represents the net amount of deferred tax liabilities after applying the valuation allowance.\n5. Portion included in non-current assets: This shows the percentage of deferred tax liabilities that are accounted for as part of noncurrent assets.\n6. Gross non-current deferred tax liability: This represents the total amount of deferred tax liabilities, including both current and non-current components, without considering any applicable adjustments.\n7. Cumulative Effect, Period of Adoption, Adjustment: This shows the cumulative effect adjustment related to the adoption of a new standard or interpretation.\n\nThis schedule is most relevant to entities that have lease assets on their balance sheet.\n\nThe relationship between this schedule and other schedules is as follows:\n1. Noncurrent deferred tax asset liability (this schedule) is related to deferred tax liabilities (Schedule 8).\n2. Deferred Tax Liabilities, Gross (this schedule) is also included in Schedule 8.\n3. Less: Valuation allowance (this schedule) is related to deferred tax liabilities (Schedule 8).', 'company_name': 'COMPANY CONFORMED NAME:\t\t\tAMETEK INC/'}